Starter code:

class Solution:
    def countSubarrays(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:


=== MODEL ===
This is a straightforward sliding window check: for each middle index, verify `nums[i-1] + nums[i+1] == nums[i] / 2`, using `2 * (nums[i-1] + nums[i+1]) == nums[i]` to stay in integers.
TOOL submit_solution {"ticket_id": "Q-6607", "code": "from typing import List\n\nclass Solution:\n    def countSubarrays(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:\n        count = 0\n        for i in range(1, len(nums) - 1):\n            if 2 * (nums[i - 1] + nums[i + 1]) == nums[i]:\n                count += 1\n        return count"}

