=== MODEL ===
This is the last slot, so I'll make it count. The approach: for each element as a maximum (or minimum) of subarrays with length ≤ k, count how many subarrays it is the designated max of, using a monotonic stack for the range where it's the max (with tie-breaking), then clip the window to length ≤ k.

For index i with left extent L (number of valid starts to its left, bounded so the subarray length stays within k) and right extent R, the count of subarrays [s, e] with s in [i-a, i], e in [i, i+b], and e − s + 1 ≤ k is computed by summing over s: for each start s, the number of valid ends is min(i+b, s+k−1) − i + 1. I'll compute this in closed form with a helper that sums an arithmetic-style count.

To keep it simple and correct, I'll sum over the possible left offsets x in [0, a] (start = i − x), where the number of ends is min(b, k−1−x) + 1, valid only if k−1−x ≥ 0. This is a sum of a piecewise-linear function, which I compute in O(1).
TOOL submit_solution {"ticket_id": "Q-6184", "code": "from typing import List\n\nclass Solution:\n    def minMaxSubarraySum(self, nums: List[int], k: int) -> int:\n        n = len(nums)\n\n        def weighted_total(vals_sign, use_max):\n            # Sum over subarrays of length <= k of their max (use_max) or min.\n            # Designate each subarray to exactly one extreme index (tie-break by index).\n            left = [0] * n   # number of positions to the left that can extend (strict on one side)\n            right = [0] * n\n            stack = []\n            for i in range(n):\n                while stack and (\n                    nums[stack[-1]] < nums[i] if use_max else nums[stack[-1]] > nums[i]\n                ):\n                    stack.pop()\n                left[i] = i - (stack[-1] if stack else -1)\n                stack.append(i)\n            stack = []\n            for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n                while stack and (\n                    nums[stack[-1]] <= nums[i] if use_max else nums[stack[-1]] >= nums[i]\n                ):\n                    stack.pop()\n                right[i] = (stack[-1] if stack else n) - i\n                stack.append(i)\n\n            total = 0\n            for i in range(n):\n                a = left[i] - 1  # max offset to the left (start = i - x, x in [0, a])\n                b = right[i] - 1  # max offset to the right (end = i + y, y in [0, b])\n                # count subarrays with start offset x, end offset y, x+y+1 <= k\n                cnt = 0\n                for x in range(0, min(a, k - 1) + 1):\n                    ymax = min(b, k - 1 - x)\n                    cnt += ymax + 1\n                total += cnt * nums[i]\n            return total\n\n        return weighted_total(None, True) + weighted_total(None, False)\n"}

