Starter code:

class Solution:
    def maximizeSumOfWeights(self, edges: List[List[int]], k: int) -> int:


=== MODEL ===
This is a tree DP. Each node may keep at most k incident edges. Root the tree at 0 and let dp[v][0] be the best sum in v's subtree when edge to parent is not kept (so v may keep up to k child edges), and dp[v][1] when the parent edge is kept (v may keep up to k−1 child edges).

For each node, sort the gains g_c = dp[c][1] + w(v,c) − dp[c][0] over children, take the positive ones greedily up to the cap. That gives dp[v][0] = sum dp[c][0] + sum of top-k positive gains, and dp[v][1] = sum dp[c][0] + top-(k−1) positive gains, plus the parent edge weight added by the caller.

Checking example 1 by hand: root 0 with children 1 (w=4) and 2 (w=2); node 2 has children 3 (w=12) and 4 (w=6). For node 2 with k=2, children are leaves: dp[c][0]=0, dp[c][1]=0, so gains are 12 and 6, both kept: dp[2][0]=18, dp[2][1]=12+... (cap k−1=1) → 12. Root 0: child 1 gives gain 4 (dp[1][1]+4−dp[1][0]=4), child 2 gives gain dp[2][1]+2−dp[2][0]=12+2−18=−4, negative, dropped. Total dp[0][0]=18+4=22 ✓.

Complexity is O(n log n) with sorting per node, which fits the constraints. I'll use an iterative DFS to avoid recursion limits.
TOOL submit_solution {"ticket_id": "T-2737", "code": "from typing import List\n\nclass Solution:\n    def maximizeSumOfWeights(self, edges: List[List[int]], k: int) -> int:\n        n = len(edges) + 1\n        adj = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n        for u, v, w in edges:\n            adj[u].append((v, w))\n            adj[v].append((u, w))\n\n        parent = [-1] * n\n        pw = [0] * n\n        order = []\n        visited = [False] * n\n        stack = [0]\n        visited[0] = True\n        while stack:\n            v = stack.pop()\n            order.append(v)\n            for to, w in adj[v]:\n                if not visited[to]:\n                    visited[to] = True\n                    parent[to] = v\n                    pw[to] = w\n                    stack.append(to)\n\n        # dp0[v]: best in subtree of v, parent edge not kept\n        # dp1[v]: best in subtree of v, parent edge kept (so v can keep k-1 child edges)\n        dp0 = [0] * n\n        dp1 = [0] * n\n\n        for v in reversed(order):\n            base = 0\n            gains = []\n            for to, w in adj[v]:\n                if to == parent[v]:\n                    continue\n                base += dp0[to]\n                g = dp1[to] + w - dp0[to]\n                if g > 0:\n                    gains.append(g)\n            gains.sort(reverse=True)\n            dp0[v] = base + sum(gains[:k])\n            dp1[v] = base + sum(gains[:k - 1]) if k - 1 > 0 else base\n\n        return dp0[0]\n"}

