=== MODEL ===
This is LeetCode 3494 style (Brewing Potions). The known solution: for consecutive potions j-1 and j, the start offset is max over i of (prefix_time_{j-1}(i) - sum of prefix skill up to i-1 times mana[j]) — i.e., compute with a monotonic-stack-free O(n·m) approach: for each adjacent pair, gap = max_i(S[i] * mana[j-1] - P[i] * mana[j]) where S is prefix sums of skill including i... Let me derive: let P[i] = sum of skill[0..i-1], so wizard i finishes potion j-1 at start + P[i+1]*mana[j-1] at earliest. For potion j to start at t, wizard i begins at t + P[i]*mana[j] and must be ≥ finish of previous: t + P[i]*mana[j] ≥ t0 + P[i+1]*mana[j-1]. So t_j - t_{j-1} = max_i (P[i+1]*mana[j-1] - P[i]*mana[j]), over i in 0..n-1. The answer is t_{m-1} + P[n]*mana[m-1].

