=== MODEL ===
This is a shortest-path problem over 4-digit states (with leading zeros allowed, since digits are modified in place). The cost of a path is the sum of all values visited, including the start and end, so I'll use Dijkstra where the cost of entering a state is its value.

Rules: both n and m must be non-prime to be feasible at the start and end; every visited state must be non-prime. If n == m and n is non-prime, the answer is n. Note the example 1 cost: 10 → 20 → 21 → 22 → 12 gives 10+20+21+22+12 = 85, which matches counting the starting value and every subsequent state.

