=== MODEL ===
This is a DP over cells, tracking a count per XOR value (values are below 16). dp[i][j][x] = number of paths from (0,0) to (i,j) whose XOR is x, including grid[i][j]. Transitions come from above and left, XORing in the current cell. The answer is dp[m-1][n-1][k]. Complexity is 300·300·16 ≈ 1.4M operations, which is fine.
TOOL submit_solution {"ticket_id": "Q-7341", "code": "from typing import List\n\nclass Solution:\n    def countPathsWithXorValue(self, grid: List[List[int]], k: int) -> int:\n        MOD = 10 ** 9 + 7\n        m, n = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n        V = 16\n        prev = None\n        for i in range(m):\n            cur = [[0] * V for _ in range(n)]\n            for j in range(n):\n                v = grid[i][j]\n                if i == 0 and j == 0:\n                    cur[0][v] = 1\n                    continue\n                for x in range(V):\n                    cnt = 0\n                    if i > 0:\n                        cnt += prev[j][x ^ v]\n                    if j > 0:\n                        cnt += cur[j - 1][x ^ v]\n                    cur[j][x] = cnt % MOD\n            prev = cur\n        return prev[n - 1][k] % MOD\n"}

