=== MODEL ===
Approach: the sum element S is some value in nums, and the remaining n−1 elements contain the n−2 specials plus the outlier. So for each candidate sum value S (by value, with count), the other elements must include one outlier O such that sum(rest) = S + O... more precisely: total T = sum(nums). If S is the sum element and O the outlier, then specials sum = S, and T = S + S + O, so O = T − 2S. For each distinct value S in nums, compute O = T − 2S, check O exists in nums at a distinct index from S (if O == S, need count ≥ 2). Return the maximum valid O.

