=== MODEL ===
This needs a DP over the array, since the operations only ever touch the first three remaining elements. I'll keep the state as the set of remaining elements from a prefix plus up to two "held back" elements. Rather than derive a closed form, I'll use a memoized DP over the remaining tuple, which is small because each step only removes from the first three.

State: a tuple of the remaining elements. Transitions: if length ≤ 2, the cost is max of remaining (or 0 if empty). Otherwise try each pair among the first three; the remaining tuple is the leftover of the first three plus nums[3:]. Since at most two elements are carried over from the first three and the rest is a suffix, the number of distinct states is O(n²), which is fine for n ≤ 1000.

