class Solution:
    def minArraySum(self, nums: List[int], k: int, op1: int, op2: int) -> int:


=== MODEL ===
With n ≤ 100, a DP over elements with state (ops1 used, ops2 used) works: dp[a][b] = minimum sum so far. For each element x, the options are: none, op1 only (ceil(x/2)), op2 only (x−k if x ≥ k), or both in either order. Order matters: op1 then op2 gives ceil(x/2) − k when ceil(x/2) ≥ k; op2 then op1 gives ceil((x−k)/2). Take the minimum of all valid options.

Check Example 1: nums [2,8,3,19,3], k=3, op1=1, op2=1. The best use is op2 on 8 (saves 3) and op1 on 19 (saves 9, 19→10). Total: 2+5+3+10+3 = 23 ✓ (the DP finds this since 9 > 3 and ops are budgeted).

