class Solution:
    def minTimeToReach(self, moveTime: List[List[int]]) -> int:


=== MODEL ===
This is a shortest-path problem where entering a room at time t requires t ≥ moveTime[i][j], so the arrival time is max(current + 1, moveTime[i][j] + 1)... more precisely, you can leave a room at time max(t, moveTime[next]) and arrive one second later. I'll use Dijkstra on arrival times.

Checking example 1: from (0,0) at t=0, leave at max(0,4)=4 to (1,0), arrive at 5; then leave to (1,1) at max(5,4)=5, arrive at 6. Output 6. Correct.

